# {{.Name}}

A declarative profile for the installed Linux Zapret/tpws backend. This source
requires the host's version-2 bypass-profile consumer; publication must set
min_app_version to the actual first host release carrying that consumer.
Unreleased source support is not a promise about deployed Sora versions.

The version-2 descriptor contains only backend (tpws on Linux, byedpi on
Windows) and 1..16 named protobuf BypassStrategy profiles. The extension-local
profile setting selects one. No paths, shell arguments, scripts, downloaded
executables or arbitrary engine config fragments are accepted.

The user grants dangerous net.hooks permission, resolves competing holders,
then explicitly connects the profile from the extension or mode picker.
Installation alone does not connect. Manual bypass settings stay separate.
Changing a selected profile reapplies the connection through the authenticated
core API; disabling or removing it disconnects without choosing a substitute.
Core validation and existing native backend constraints still apply.

Windows WinDivert/winws is a different backend and is not supplied here.
This extension does not add a driver, MITM certificate, or access to VPN keys.

Build and sign with the ordinary author-key and team-catalog review flow:
sora-ext validate; sora-ext pack . -o {{.ID}}.soraext;
sora-ext sign --key .sora/author.key {{.ID}}.soraext.
Production signing and publication are separate authorized operations.
